3. [x] Exclude `.env`, local environments, generated assets, and model weights from Git/Docker publishing.
4. [x] Make API startup independent of model availability; verify health returns 200 and missing-model prediction returns 503.
5. [ ] Obtain Azure subscription ID and deployment region; confirm resource group name.
6. [ ] Validate Azure region/SKU availability and generate Bicep infrastructure files.
7. [ ] Build and scan the container image; provision Azure resources.
8. [ ] Upload/mount model weights, configure secrets, deploy, and validate app endpoints in Azure.
9. [ ] Create/push the public GitHub repository after confirming repository owner and reviewing the public file list.

